From 2d0ea0adff655da992ec4d4f11027f9cff1f8540 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian MacDonald <ian@netstatz.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 17:55:22 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 73/92] fix(classify): no replay after a crash on text, refuse
 labels, no linked cache

Text classification replayed an input once after it crashed the backend,
and had no crash breaker, so an input that kills a CPU engine could keep
it in a crash-and-reload loop. It now takes the image route's path: the
input is not retried (502 backend_crashed_on_input), and three crashes in
60 seconds pause the model for 60 seconds (503 backend_crash_cooldown,
checked before any auto-load). Text and image share one breaker per model.
This also covers ort-server text classification and the router's
classifier helpers, which call Router::classify.

The tflite and executorch text adapters dropped a request's labels and
returned the model's fixed classes with 200. They now refuse labels with
400, as the classify route documents.

tflite-server writes its weight cache through a symlink, which in an HF
snapshot points into the shared blob store, so lemond passes
--weight-cache only when that path is missing or a plain file.

The fake tflite-server gains a text mode and logs its arguments, for the
new tests.

